        "## Composite parameters\n",
        "\n",
        "| Parameter | Value |\n",
        "|---|---|\n",
        "| Source | Landsat Collection 2 Level-2, Microsoft Planetary Computer |\n",
        "| Collection | `landsat-c2-l2` |\n",
        "| Platform | Landsat 8 only |\n",
        "| Temporal window | Full calendar year |\n",
        "| Cloud cover filter | < 30 % (scene level) |\n",
        "| Resolution | 30 m (native) |\n",
        "| CRS | EPSG:25830 (ETRS89 / UTM 30N) |\n",
        "| Years compared | 2020 and 2025 |\n",
        "| Area of interest | Asturias, all 78 concejos dissolved |\n",
        "\n",
        "### Why these values\n",
        "\n",
        "**Landsat 8 only.** The `landsat-c2-l2` collection holds all Landsat missions.\n",
        "Landsat 5 (TM), 7 (ETM+) and 8/9 (OLI) carry different sensors, and Landsat 7 has\n",
        "suffered scan line corrector failure since 2003, producing striped imagery. Using a\n",
        "single platform in both years removes cross-sensor calibration as a source of\n",
        "difference. Landsat 9 is excluded although it would add observations in 2025, because\n",
        "it did not exist in 2020 and would make the two years unequal in sensor composition.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Full calendar year, not a fixed seasonal window.** A summer-only window was tested\n",
        "first and rejected on the data: at < 30 % cloud it left as few as 1 scene per WRS-2\n",
        "tile in 2025, which makes a median meaningless. The full year was then checked for the\n",
        "seasonal bias a fixed window was meant to prevent, and the two years proved balanced:\n",
        "\n",
        "| Check | 2020 | 2025 |\n",
        "|---|---|---|\n",
        "| Scenes | 40 | 34 |\n",
        "| Scenes per tile | 7–9 | 6–9 |\n",
        "| Mean sun elevation | 46.2° | 46.0° |\n",
        "| Sun elevation std | 15.7 | 14.3 |\n",
        "| Leaf-off share (Nov–Apr) | 35.0 % | 38.2 % |\n",
        "\n",
        "**Cloud threshold identical in both years.** The threshold decides which scenes enter\n",
        "the composite. Different thresholds would mean differently selected data and\n",
        "non-comparable results, regardless of how each composite looks on its own.\n",
        "\n",
        "**EPSG:25830 stated explicitly, not `crs='utm'`.** Asturias straddles the boundary\n",
        "between UTM zones 29N and 30N at 6° W. Landsat scenes are projected into the zone of\n",
        "their own centre, so scenes covering the same region arrive in different zones.\n",
        "`crs='utm'` would resolve to a single zone chosen from the data; stating ETRS89 /\n",
        "UTM 30N makes the choice explicit and matches the official Spanish CRS for the mainland.\n",
        "\n",
        "**30 m is native resolution.** Requesting a finer grid would resample without adding\n",
        "detail and increase data volume quadratically.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Known limitations\n",
        "\n",
        "- Asturias is covered by five WRS-2 tiles (202/030, 203/029, 203/030, 204/029,\n",
        "  204/030) with uneven scene counts, so the number of observations behind each pixel\n",
        "  of the composite varies across the region. Areas in the sidelap between adjacent\n",
        "  paths are observed roughly twice as often as areas within a single path.\n",
        "- Scene-level `eo:cloud_cover` describes a 185 × 180 km footprint and does not\n",
        "  indicate cloud over any particular part of Asturias. Per-pixel masking from the\n",
        "  `qa_pixel` band would be required for that.\n",
        "- Composites represent typical annual condition, not any single date."
